Z||000000||ThatRickGuy||10-11-2000||06:50 PM||||Hey, I was just talking to my machinest, she really excited about get my engine (the 3.2) going because her shop hasn't put anything like it together befor, and they just got another guy asking about it for a fiero (anyone here talking to Dian at Norpa?) anyways, she mentioned something to me that I know I've seen in the boards. The lower intake manifold is aluminum, the block is cast, the two don't like eachother. She said that after the initial break in and road run, that the intake will loosen itself up, that I'll have to go threw and re-torque the bolts. then again between 500-1000 miles check it. she said after the 2nd or possibly 3rd time retightening these to 40lbs (I beleive) the shouldn't move, but you should feel like a little click that is bassically how the settle and they should be good from then on. Signs that can indicate that your intake is starting to losen up a bit would be a vaccumm leak, a single puff of black smoke on start up (like when you have worn rings) and eventually degraded performance. Just a tip to hopefully save some of you guys some hunting and or gasket replacement.||||reg||3
